          "unit_id": "get_it_fixed",
          "title": "The Boiler",
          "description": "Encarga que te hagan cosas: have / get something done.",
          "lessons": [
            {
              "lesson_id": "get_it_fixed_lesson",
              "title": "Causative have and get",
              "steps": [
                {
                  "phase": "context",
                  "type": "audio_context",
                  "content": {
                    "title": "The boiler",
                    "dialogue": [
                      {
                        "speaker": "Mrs Green",
                        "text": "I'm having the boiler repaired on Thursday. The engineer can't come any earlier."
                      },
                      {
                        "speaker": "Priya",
                        "text": "Thursday? We haven't had hot water since Sunday!"
                      },
                      {
                        "speaker": "Mrs Green",
                        "text": "I know, dear. And while I'm at it, I'm getting the kitchen repainted next month."
                      },
                      {
                        "speaker": "Ollie",
                        "text": "Could you have the oven checked too? It's been making a strange noise."
                      },
                      {
                        "speaker": "Mrs Green",
                        "text": "Fine. I'll get someone to look at it."
                      },
                      {
                        "speaker": "Lucía",
                        "text": "Meanwhile, I'm going to shower at the gym. I might get my hair cut while I'm there."
                      },
                      {
                        "speaker": "Priya",
                        "text": "Good plan. I had my car serviced last week, so at least the heating in the car works."
                      },
                      {
                        "speaker": "Mrs Green",
                        "text": "You young people. In my day, we had the chimney swept and lit a fire."
                      },
                      {
                        "speaker": "Ollie",
                        "text": "Shall I make some soup to keep us warm?"
                      },
                      {
                        "speaker": "Mrs Green",
                        "text": "Now that's the best idea I've heard all day."
                      }
                    ],
                    "passage": "February. The boiler at Clifton Road breaks down during the coldest week of the year. Mrs Green comes round."
                  }
                },
                {
                  "phase": "discovery",
                  "type": "multiple_choice",
                  "content": {
                    "instructions": "Fíjate en el diálogo y responde.",
                    "items": [
                      {
                        "question": "\"I'm having the boiler repaired.\" Who repairs it?",
                        "options": [
                          "an engineer",
                          "Mrs Green"
                        ],
                        "answer": 0
                      },
                      {
                        "question": "The structure is…",
                        "options": [
                          "have + object + past participle",
                          "have + past participle + object"
                        ],
                        "answer": 0
                      },
                      {
                        "question": "\"I'll get someone to look at it.\" get + person + …",
                        "options": [
                          "to + verb",
                          "-ing"
                        ],
                        "answer": 0
                      },
                      {
                        "question": "Why can't the boiler be repaired earlier?",
                        "options": [
                          "The engineer can't come any earlier.",
                          "It's too expensive.",
                          "Mrs Green is away."
                        ],
                        "answer": 0
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                },
                {
                  "phase": "grammar",
                  "type": "grammar_rule",
                  "content": {
                    "title": "Causative have and get",
                    "explanation": "Have / get + objeto + participio indica que otra persona hace algo por nosotros, normalmente un servicio: I'm having the boiler repaired (no lo arreglo yo). Get es más informal.\n\nSe usa en cualquier tiempo: I had my car serviced last week. I'm getting the kitchen repainted. Could you have the oven checked?\n\nPara decir a quién le encargas algo: get + persona + to + verbo (I'll get someone to look at it) o have + persona + verbo (I'll have the engineer call you).\n\nEn español solemos decir «me voy a cortar el pelo», pero en inglés es I'm going to get my hair cut, porque te lo corta otra persona.",
                    "table": {
                      "headers": [
                        "Estructura",
                        "Ejemplo"
                      ],
                      "rows": [
                        [
                          "have + objeto + participio",
                          "I'm having the boiler repaired."
                        ],
                        [
                          "get + objeto + participio",
                          "I'm getting the kitchen repainted."
                        ],
                        [
                          "pasado",
                          "I had my car serviced last week."
                        ],
                        [
                          "con modal",
                          "Could you have the oven checked?"
                        ],
                        [
                          "get + persona + to + verbo",
                          "I'll get someone to look at it."
                        ],
                        [
                          "have + persona + verbo",
                          "I'll have the engineer call you."
                        ]
                      ]
                    },
                    "examples": [
                      "I'm having the boiler repaired on Thursday.",
                      "I'm getting the kitchen repainted next month.",
                      "Could you have the oven checked too?",
                      "I might get my hair cut while I'm there."
                    ]
                  }
                },
